					<hr width="75%" align="left">
					<div class="xsmall"><a href="http://www.guildsay.com/guilds/view_character.php?id=2882">Serenna Nytefyrre</a></div><div class="xsmall"><a href="http://www.guildsay.com/guilds/view_character.php?id=2588">Laine L`ssinurn</a></div><div class="xsmall"><a href="http://www.guildsay.com/guilds/view_character.php?id=3170">Teriel L`ssinurn</a></div><div class="xsmall"><a href="http://www.guildsay.com/guilds/view_character.php?id=3103">Ellewinne</a></div><div class="xsmall"><a href="http://www.guildsay.com/guilds/view_character.php?id=3214">Rathil</a></div><div class="xsmall"><a href="http://www.guildsay.com/guilds/view_character.php?id=3213">Terial</a></div>					
					<br>
				</td>
				<td width="70%" class="body" valign="top">
					<table width="100%" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="0" border="0">
					<tr>
						<td width="100%" class="body" valign="top">
														This kind of goes along with the saying, &quot;The only dumb question is the one you do not ask.&quot;<br />
<br />
Like Saddori stated, every player has a role within a group that they are expected to perform, for the safety and benefit of the whole group. The Order of Nobleshadows guild is partially based upon helping out a fellow man or woman to find their place in Norrath. Learning effective strategies about whichever class you have chosen to play is apart of finding your niche. Post away, no one here will look down upon you, however trivial the question may seem.						</td>
